<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Romsdal</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Romsdal is a traditional district of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> around the Romsdalsfjord, in the county of Møre og Romsdal, with Molde and Åndalsnes as its main towns. It is known for steep mountains, including the Trollveggen rock wall. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viking-age">Viking Age</a> it formed part of the domain of the earls of Møre.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/romsdal.jpg" alt="Romsdal" width="320" height="236" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pilum at English Wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Romsdal-region.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
